out.push(S('Stage 7 · Write freely – exam practice (Writing Part 1: the essay, sample 178 words)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Do written rules at work solve more problems than they create?**',
  '**They solve more than they create, but only when they are written so that they can be failed, and most of the rules I have met cannot be.**',
  '**The case for clarity is easy to make and easy to overstate. A line that says _no carton is to show a crush of more than ten millimetres_ ends an argument in four seconds, because two people looking at the same carton with the same rule reach the same answer. A line that says _the packaging must be undamaged_ does the opposite: it produces two honest readings and two hours at a gate, and the person holding the clipboard pays for both of them.**',
  '**The cost of writing them is real and it is not the writing. It is the twenty minutes of asking the person who does the work what the process can actually hold, and that is the step everybody leaves out.**',
  '**My own third point is the one I had not expected. A written rule cannot ask. It is written by the party who applies it and met by the party who cannot change it, so the silence that comes back is read as agreement when it is nothing of the kind.**',
  '**So the rules are worth having, and the sentence that makes them worth having is the one inviting the objection.**',
]));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The essay above is a band-5 answer and the third note is where it earns the mark.** **A general observation about bureaucracy would have been competent and unremarkable; _a written rule cannot ask_ is the unit\'s own finding and it is specific, arguable and short.** ⚠ **Teach the habit directly: in Part 1 the two given notes are the floor and the third note is the whole difference between a safe answer and a good one.** **And mark the first sentence hardest.** **The question is answered in it, with the condition attached** — _only when they are written so that they can be failed_ — **and an essay that reaches its position in the fourth paragraph has lost marks that the content never recovers.**'));
out.push(S('Stage ✓ · Unit 21 check'));
out.push(A('**A** **1** a _(specification)_   **2** b _(tolerance)_   **3** c _(verification)_   **4** a _(definition)_   **5** b _(inspection)_   **6** c _(deviation)_   **7** a _(confirmation)_   **8** c _(adoption)_'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 3 is the item that separates a class.** **_The card carries no ___ of the batch at either end_ needs the abstract noun, and a room that has just met nine of them still reaches for the past participle because _verified_ sounds right after _no_.** **Read it aloud and the error is audible.** ⚠ **Item 5 is the pair to put beside it:** **_the inspection of 9 May_ is an event with a date, and _the inspecting of 9 May_ is not English** — **which is the general rule worth stating once: when the word takes a date, it takes the noun.**'));
out.push(A('**B  Listening** **1** B   **2** C   **3** A   **4** C   **5** A   **6** C   **7** B   **8** B'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 3 is the one to replay.** **Two of the three options are mentioned in the extract** — **an instrument is named and a sample is counted** — **but the question is what they agree a method must _do_, and the answer is the repeatability sentence: _you could do it tomorrow and get my answer._** **Students choose B because the instrument is the last thing they hear.** ⚠ **Item 7 is the other replay, and it is the finding of the whole unit in nine seconds.** **The man says explicitly that the supplier was not being dishonest but commercial, and students choose C because the silence feels like a concealment.** **Replay it and ask whose decision the silence was, and the answer arrives.**'));
out.push(A('**C  Writing** — **marked on the six parts and on the definitions.** ⚠ **A specification with excellent criteria and no scope has failed the first requirement**, **and it is the commonest loss by a long way.** **The second commonest is a consequence that does not name a clause number, which makes the page unusable by anybody who has not read it.** **The Stage 7 sample in 21.6 above is the band-5 model.**'));
